NNLO QCD corrections to leptonic observables in top-quark pair production and decay

Fiducial phase space corresponding to section 3.3 in JHEP 05 (2021) 212 (arxiv:2008.11133)
Inclusive phase corresponds to partonic tops only.
All cross section are normalised to the total cross section.
Scale/PDF variations are computed in a correleted way, i.e. the cross sections are normalised for each scale/PDF choice and the variation is taken from the resulting bands.

Authors: Czakon, Mitov, Poncelet

Contact:  mczakon@physik.rwth-aachen.de
          adm74@cam.ac.uk
          poncelet@hep.phy.cam.ac.uk

Model parameters:
mt = 172.5 GeV
mW = 80.385 GeV
mZ = 91.1876 GeV
GW = 2.0928 GeV
Gt = (1.48063 - 1.18*aS - 2.65*aS^2) GeV
GF = 1.166379*10^-5 GeV^-2
nf = 5 (massless b-quarks)

PDF:
  LO   : NNPDF31_lo_as_0118
  NLO  : NNPDF31_nlo_as_0118
  NNLO : NNPDF31_nnlo_as_0118

Scales: muR = HT/4, muF = HT/4

All histograms are given as a list of bins with the data format in case of absolute distributions ([X]: energy unit of observable):

Units : [X]      [X]       1/[X]         1/[X]    1/[X]      1/[X]         1/[X]  1/[X]
Values: edge-low edge-high scale_central scale_up scale_down mcerr_central PDF_up  PDF_down

in case of 2D (and analogously for 3D):

